      "examples": [
        {
          "exampleId": "w:wetland#e-f832b3eb452efbc3",
          "text": "“It sounds crazy to talk about guilt-free fur-unless you understand that the nutria are destroying vast wetlands every year”, says Cree McCree, project director of Righteous Fur.",
          "source": {
            "paperId": "paper-gaokao-2020-national-ii",
            "paperTitle": "2020年普通高等学校招生全国统一考试英语（全国Ⅱ卷）",
            "groupId": "group:paper-gaokao-2020-national-ii:reading-c",
            "locator": {
              "paragraph": 2,
              "paragraphId": "block:paper-gaokao-2020-national-ii:reading-c:2",
              "sentence": 2
            }
          },
          "tier": "gaokao",
          "target": {
            "start": 104,
            "end": 112
          }
        },
        {
          "exampleId": "w:wetland#e-886fff6bf4d8e8b3",
          "text": "In 1934, with the passage of the Migratory Bird Hunting Stamp Act (Act), an increasingly concerned nation took firm action to stop the destruction of migratory (迁徙的) waterfowl and the wetlands so vital to their survival.",
          "source": {
            "paperId": "paper-gaokao-2021-i",
            "paperTitle": "2021年普通高等学校招生全国统一考试英语",
            "groupId": "group:paper-gaokao-2021-i:reading-c",
            "locator": {
              "paragraph": 3,
              "paragraphId": "block:paper-gaokao-2021-i:reading-c:3",
              "sentence": 1
            }
          },
          "tier": "gaokao",
          "target": {
            "start": 184,
            "end": 192
          }
        },
        {
          "exampleId": "w:wetland#e-c896fa292d0ac5d4",
          "text": "About 98 cents of every duck stamp dollar goes directly into the Migratory Bird Conservation Fund to purchase wetlands and wildlife habitat for inclusion into the National Wildlife Refuge System – a fact that ensures this land will be protected and available for all generations to come.",
          "source": {
            "paperId": "paper-gaokao-2021-i",
